hed, even\n157:\\code{v2}, so second-half revenue is $260-110=150$. Subtracting the original\n176:$\\alpha=F/100$. With the floating rate resetting to 7\\%, interest is\n199:The joint symbolic result is cash $93.6+1.6\\alpha$, profit\n219:It records internal cross-references and externally incorporated material,\n225:every incorporated external document.\n232:85,750. Fair value is separately disclosed as 88.4 billion. None of these\n235:Note 9 identifies the notes as fixed-rate, then states that interest-rate\n236:swaps effectively convert a portion to floating rates. Note 4 reports\n237:interest-rate contract notional of 14,575 at the annual date. A notional is\n239:interest sensitivity: reset timing, remaining periods, curve conventions and\n250:To demonstrate a source-to-forecast calculation, freeze the interim balance\n252:period: a 200-basis-point rate increase, no principal change, no offsetting\n255:produces $0.02\\times(13/52)E=72.875$ million additional interest. This exposure\n257:interim net sensitivity. Under that condition, debit interest expense and\n264:conditional added interest lies in $[0,72.875]$ before monetary rounding. That\n267:coherent marginal propagation. Northstar supplies the complete-company\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
