{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,90p' tests/test_accounting_p04.py; sed -n '1,62p' tests/test_accounting_p03.py; sed -n '1,78p' docs/design/chapters/07-execution.tex\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,90p' tests/test_accounting_p04.py; sed -n '1,62p' tests/test_accounting_p03.py; sed -n '1,78p' docs/design/chapters/07-execution.tex\"","aggregated_output":"\"\"\"Independent input replay and exact algebra; P04 executed obligations.\"\"\"\nimport copy\nfrom contextlib import redirect_stderr, redirect_stdout\nfrom dataclasses import replace\nfrom fractions import Fraction as F\nfrom itertools import product\nimport json\nimport hashlib\nimport io\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport sys\nimport tempfile\nimport unittest\nfrom unittest.mock import patch\nsys.path.insert(0,str(Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]/'scripts'))\nimport z3\nfrom rational_solver_v1 import *\nfrom reconstruction_v1 import *\nfrom test_accounting_p03 import bindings, BASE\nfrom core0_frontends_v1 import compile_source\nROOT=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]\nOBSERVATIONS=[]\nB=Budget(20,10000,500,500,20000,1000,1000000)\n\n\ndef spec():\n    return json.loads((ROOT/'docs/design/fixtures/p04-reconstruction-cases-v1.json').read_text())['input_fixture']\n\n\ndef observation(s,amount):\n    return {'id':'cash-note','context':copy.deepcopy(s['context']),'action':'Accept','source':['synthetic:cash-note'],\n            'mapping':'cash','domain':{'lower':str(amount),'upper':str(amount),'lower_closed':True,'upper_closed':True}}\n\n\nclass ReconstructionTests(unittest.TestCase):\n    def record(self,name,result):OBSERVATIONS.append({'obligation':name,'passed':True,'result':result})\n    def test_independent_enumeration(self):\n        evidence=[]\n        # Oracle replays original template incidence; no production expressions or Z3.\n        for opening,total,limit,coefficient in [(10,13,3,1),(4,8,4,1),(7,13,3,2)]:\n            s=spec();s['opening']={'Cash':str(opening),'Equity':str(-opening)}\n            s['templates']['sale']['postings']={'Cash':str(coefficient),'Equity':str(-coefficient)}\n            for row in s['slots']:row['integer_bounds']=[0,limit]\n            s['observations']=[observation(s,total)]\n            p=construct(s);r=solve(p,B)\n            actual={(int(F(c['witness']['a'])),int(F(c['witness']['b']))) for c in r['cells'] if c['feasibility']=='sat'}\n            expected=set()\n            for a,b in product(range(limit+1),repeat=2):\n                cash=F(opening)\n                for amount in (a,b):cash+=F(coefficient)*amount\n                if cash==total:expected.add((a,b))\n            self.assertEqual(actual,expected);self.assertEqual(r['status'],'ExactWithinScope')\n            for c in r['cells']:\n                if c['feasibility']=='sat':self.assertEqual(F(c['outputs']['cash'])+F(c['outputs']['equity']),0)\n            s['slots'].reverse();rr=solve(construct(s),B)\n            self.assertEqual({tuple(c['witness'][n] for n in ('a','b')) for c in rr['cells'] if c['feasibility']=='sat'},\n                             {tuple(c['witness'][n] for n in ('a','b')) for c in r['cells'] if c['feasibility']=='sat'})\n            evidence.append({'inputs':s,'oracle':sorted(expected),'actual':r})\n        self.record('enumeration',evidence)\n    def test_p03_parent_views(self):\n        source=BASE.replace('alternative allFixed { assume alpha == 1; }','alternative allFixed { assume alpha <= 0.75; }').replace('alternative allFloating { assume alpha == 0; }','alternative allFloating { assume alpha >= 0.25; }')\n        results=[]\n        for text in (BASE,source):\n            c=compile_source(text,bindings());self.assertTrue(c.ok)\n            p=from_p03(c.ir,bindings(),{'DemoDebt@1/DebtMix':'fixed-floating-amounts-v1'})\n            self.assertFalse(p.unsupported)\n            r=solve(p,B,p.outputs['interest']);self.assertEqual(r['bounds']['lower']['value'],'5');self.assertEqual(r['bounds']['upper']['value'],'7')\n            self.assertEqual(r['coverage']['total'],1)\n            half=p.variables['alpha']==q('1/2')\n            self.assertEqual(solve(p,B,extra=[half])['feasibility'],'Feasible')\n            both=solve(p,B,selected_views=['allFixed','allFloating'],view_operator='intersection',extra=[half])\n            self.assertEqual(both['feasibility'],'Infeasible' if text==BASE else 'Feasible')\n            fixed=solve(p,B,selected_views=['allFixed'],extra=[half])\n            self.assertEqual(fixed['feasibility'],'Infeasible' if text==BASE else 'Feasible')\n            self.assertEqual(solve(p,B,extra=[half])['feasibility'],'Feasible')\n            results.append({'parent':r,'intersection':both,'conditional':fixed})\n        self.record('p03_views',results)\n    def test_rounded_strict_and_unbounded(self):\n        fixture=json.loads((ROOT/'docs/design/fixtures/borrowings.json').read_text())['rounded']\n        p=Problem('rounded-debt','fixture');f,v=z3.Reals('F V');p.variables={'F':f,'V':v}\n        p.add('amounts',z3.And(f>=0,v>=0));p.add('debt-note',z3.And(f+v>=q(fixture['debt'][0]),f+v<q(fixture['debt'][1])))\n        p.add('interest-note',z3.And(q('.05')*(f+v)>=q(fixture['interest'][0]),q('.05')*(f+v)<q(fixture['interest'][1])))\n        r=solve(p,B,q('.05')*f+q('.07')*v)\n        self.assertEqual(r['bounds']['lower']['value'],'199/40');self.assertTrue(r['bounds']['lower']['attained'])\n        self.assertEqual(r['bounds']['upper']['value'],'1407/200');self.assertFalse(r['bounds']['upper']['attained'])\n        x=z3.Real('x');empty=Problem('empty','fixture',variables={'x':x});empty.add('strict',x>0);empty.add('closed',x<=0)\n        self.assertEqual(solve(empty,B,x)['status'],'Infeasible')\n        u=Problem('unbounded','fixture',variables={'x':x});u.add('positive',x>0)\n        un=solve(u,B,x);self.assertEqual(un['bounds']['upper']['status'],'Unbounded');self.assertFalse(un['bounds']['lower']['attained'])\n        const=solve(u,B,q(2));self.assertTrue(const['bounds']['lower']['attained'])\n\"\"\"Executed P03 obligations; authored typed inputs never pass through the parser.\"\"\"\nimport copy\nfrom dataclasses import replace\nfrom fractions import Fraction as F\nimport hashlib\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport sys\nimport tempfile\nimport unittest\nfrom unittest.mock import patch\n\nROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]\nsys.path.insert(0, str(ROOT / 'scripts'))\nimport core0_ir_v1 as ir\nfrom core0_frontends_v1 import compile_source\nimport jsonschema\n\nOBSERVATIONS = []\nBASE = (ROOT / 'docs/design/fixtures/borrowing.acc').read_text()\nREASON = 'Fixed-rate proportion not disclosed'\nRENAMED = '''module FinancingStudy version \"2\";\nuse DemoDebt version \"1\";\nsource disclosure = external(\"synthetic-note-7\");\nentity Beta functional USD;\nbook Statutory entity Beta basis DemoDebt version \"1\";\naccount Cash : Asset book Statutory;\naccount Debt : Liability book Statutory;\naccount InterestExpense : Expense book Statutory;\naccount Retained : Equity book Statutory;\nopening carried for Statutory from external(\"after-2025-close\");\nobservation borrowing : Money<USD> instant @2025-12-31 = 150 USD from disclosure;\nsymbol share : Real in [0, 1] because \"Fixed-rate proportion not disclosed\";\ncontract facility : DebtMix book Statutory {\n principal = value(borrowing); fixed_fraction = share;\n fixed_rate = 0.05 per year; initial_floating_rate = 0.05 per year;\n}\nalternative fixed { assume share == 1; }\nalternative floating { assume share == 0; }\nscenario shock { set market_rate = constant(0.08 per year); }\nreport financials for Statutory { mapping = external(\"DemoDebt.statements.v1\"); }\n'''\n\n\ndef bindings(principal=100, renamed=False):\n    \"\"\"Explicit synthetic evidence, separately authored from source and expected IR.\"\"\"\n    p = F(principal); stamp = '2026-01-01T00:00:00Z'\n    book, symbol = ('Statutory', 'share') if renamed else ('Local', 'alpha')\n    names = ('fixed', 'floating') if renamed else ('allFixed', 'allFloating')\n    package_path = ROOT / 'docs/design/fixtures/demo-debt-package.json'\n    return ir.CompileBindings(\n        packages=[ir.PackageBinding('DemoDebt', '1', hashlib.sha256(package_path.read_bytes()).hexdigest(),\n            'DemoDebt', '2025-01-01', '2028-01-01', ['reset','accrue_and_pay','close','statements'],\n            ['builtin:Core0@1','DemoCalendar@1'], ['fixture:demo-debt-package.json'])],\n        readings=[ir.ReadingBinding('synthetic-note-7', f'Synthetic disclosed debt {p} USD; split undisclosed', p,\n            'USD', '2025-12-31', 'fixture:p03-synthetic', 'synthetic-2025', stamp, stamp,\n            'synthetic-author', stamp, 'Explicit synthetic acceptance, not human approval', stamp,\n            system_as_of=stamp, action='Accept')],\n        openings=[ir.OpeningBinding('after-2025-close', '2025-12-31',\n            {'Cash':p-5, 'Debt':-p, 'InterestExpense':0, 'Retained':5}, book=book)],\n        reports=[ir.ReportBinding('DemoDebt.statements.v1','DemoDebt.statements.v1',\n            'interest_operating','close',['accrue_and_pay'])],\n\\chapter{Reconstruction and execution procedures}\n\\label{ch:execution}\n\n\\section{Ingest, reconcile and construct histories}\n\nThe historical procedure starts with a filing manifest. It records documents,\nreporting dates, publication dates, revisions and expected statements and\nnotes. Tagged filings are parsed through an XBRL adapter; PDF and HTML sources\nare segmented into text, tables, captions and references. The original bytes\nand extraction output remain immutable. Re-running an improved extractor\ncreates a new extraction version with links to the same source.\n\nFor each table, the importer first resolves headers, units, signs, periods and\ndimensions. It then proposes concept mappings. A deterministic validator checks\nsubtotal arithmetic, duplicate facts, comparative consistency and cross-note\nreferences. Every proposed repair creates a new reading. The system may suggest\nthat an OCR value is 10 rather than 70, but only a reviewed correction or an\nexplicit alternative allows that reading into a validated model.\n\nReconciliation proceeds from local totals to movement schedules. A debt bridge\nmay contain opening debt, issuance, repayment, acquired debt, interest\naccretion, currency effects, fair-value changes and closing debt. Every\ncomponent receives a movement type. An unexplained residual is stored as a\nresidual with a source and period; it is not automatically classified as\nrepayment or issuance. A model can introduce an unknown decomposition of that\nresidual, subject to evidence and economic constraints.\n\nThe reconstruction engine then performs the following finite procedure within\na declared model scope:\n\\begin{enumerate}\n\\item Build shared variables for observations, opening states, contract terms\nand supported movement amounts. Attach original rounding domains.\n\\item Add identities, roll-forwards, account restrictions, contractual\nrelationships and cross-period links. Add each semantic reading as a condition\non the same joint model.\n\\item Propagate types, units, intervals and simple equalities. Reject context\nmismatches before invoking a numerical solver.\n\\item Ask the solver for feasibility. On infeasibility, return a sufficient\nconflicting subset of constraints, its source spans and model assumptions.\nA solver's conflict core need not be the smallest possible explanation.\n\\item Retain finite alternatives and continuous solution families symbolically.\nMaterialise example histories only when needed for review or execution.\n\\item Check whether each requested simulation has sufficient economic state.\nMissing maturities, reset dates or cohort composition become declared\nassumptions or explicit unresolved inputs.\n\\end{enumerate}\n\nUnrestricted journal enumeration would be unbounded: arbitrary offsetting\ntransactions can be inserted without changing reports. The model therefore\ndeclares allowed event types, time resolution, relevant accounts, lot/cohort\nresolution and limits on latent contract instances. These limits describe the\nrepresented family; they are not evidence that all real possibilities were\nsearched. The compiler canonicalises syntactic duplicates and equivalences\nestablished by its supported rewrite rules. It does not decide arbitrary\neconomic equivalence. Probability measures attach to declared economic\nhypotheses or parameters, never to a count of encodings; adding a duplicate\nrepresentation therefore cannot create extra probability mass or coverage.\n\nThe first implementation uses symbolic linear bridges and finite structural\nchoices. Nonlinear economic models can be evaluated on feasible states through\nplugins. A solver timeout preserves the unresolved family and returns\n\\code{SolverIncomplete}; it does not prune the family as impossible. Search\nbudgets belong to run configuration and are recorded with the results.\n\n\\section{Condition a run without rewriting history}\n\nA run selects an evidence view and cutoff, a historical family, a forecast\nstarting date, scenario definitions, accounting packages, management policies,\noutput queries and numerical settings. A run may use a concrete history,\nan exact symbolic family, a finite set of conditional histories, or weighted\ndraws from a declared distribution. The output records which mode was used.\n\nSuppose no debt maturity is disclosed. An analyst may run a conditional case\nthat assumes all debt matures after the forecast horizon. The run is valid\nunder that assumption even though the historical representation remains\nincomplete. The interface must display the assumption next to the result and\nprovide sensitivity cases when the assumption is material. It must not label\nthe assumed maturity as a discovered historical fact.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
